   ```
   // error.ts

   import { NextFunction, Request, Response } from "express";

   export function errorhandler(_: any, err: Error, __: Request, res: Response, ___: NextFunction) {
     res.status(500).json({ error: err.message });
   }
   ```

11. In your `main.ts` file, add your middleware:

   ```typescript
   import errorhandler from "./middleware/error";

   app.use(errorhandler);
   ```

12. Finally, run your server:

   ```bash
   npx ts-node src/main.ts
   ```

   You should see the server listening on port 3000.

   Note: Remember to replace `process.env.PORT` with an actual port number, or use an environment variable to supply it.

   You can also add nodemon as a devDependency to auto-restart your server when you make changes to your code:

   ```
   npm install --save-dev nodemon
   ```

   And add the following to your `package.json` file:

   ```json
   {
     "scripts": {
       "dev": "nodemon src/main.ts"
     }
   }
   ```

   Now you can run `npm run dev` to start your server in development mode, and it will recompile and restart automatically whenever you modify your typescript files.

