Here is a custom ESLint rule for Vue.js that will enforce best practices regarding updating lifecycle hook methods and call methods that modify internal component state:

```javascript
// eslint-disable-next-line no-unused-vars
module.exports = {
  rules: {
    'vue-modify-internals-state': {
      meta: {
        docs: {
          description: 'Enforce not modifying internal component state within lifecycle hook methods and prevent calling methods that modify internal component state.',
          category: 'Vue.js',
          recommended: true,
        },
        fixable: null,
        schema: [],
      },
      create(context) {
        return {
          // Handle updated lifecycle hook methods
          'FunctionDeclaration:(expression|declaration)([^)]*):updated()': (node) => {
            const methodName = node.id.name;
            const internalComponentsModifierMethods = ['push', 'splice', 'sort', 'reverse']; // Add more methods as needed
            const callExpressions = node.body.body.filter((nestedNode) => nestedNode.type === 'ExpressionStatement');

            // Check if method modifies internal component state
            if (internalComponentsModifierMethods.includes(methodName)) {
              context.report({
                node,
                message: `Don't modify internal component state within ${methodName} lifecycle hook.`
              });
            }

            // Check if method calls a method that modifies internal component state
            callExpressions.forEach((expressionStatement) => {
              const calleeNode = expressionStatement.expression.callee;
              if ( calleeNode.type === 'MemberExpression' && internalComponentsModifierMethods.includes(calleeNode.property.name) ) {
                context.report({
                  node: expressionStatement,
                  message: `Don't call methods that modify internal component state within ${methodName} lifecycle hook.`
                });
              }
            });
          },
        },
      },
    },
  },
};
```

This rule will detect updated() lifecycle hook methods that modify internal component state using the `push`, `splice`, `sort`, and `reverse` methods, and report warnings. It will also detect call expressions within updated() lifecycle hook methods that call methods that modify internal component state, and report warnings. 

To use this custom ESLint rule, add it to your .eslintrc.js file:

```javascript
module.exports = {
  extends: [
    'eslint:recommended',
    'plugin:vue/recommended',
  ],
  plugins: ['vue'],
  rules: {
    'vue-modify-internals-state': 'error',
    // ...other rules
  },
};
``` 

